Z||000003||Lore||04-21-2001||12:25 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroJoe:<BR><B>Sounds like a very nice car!  Do you have any pics of it?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>No, unfortunately I don't have any pics of it yet, although hopefully I will be getting some soon.  <P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Rashaam:<BR><B>Where in Japan did you live? I am moving over there next March, but I am going to bring my Fiero.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Right now I live in a small town on the southern tip of the island called Sasebo.  I would of brought my Fiero over but they told me that if the car was made after 1977 or something like that, it couldn't be brought over.  Anything before that is considered an "antique".  I'm not sure why they made that rule.  Some people say it has to do with the pollution but that makes no sense because cars after 1977 produce much less pollution than cars before 1977.  Maybe you can talk some sense in 'em and be able to take your Fiero over there.    <P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Rashaam||04-22-2001||11:13 AM||||I already got all the info on importing the car. They must have changed the rule cause now the car just has to comply with the emissions for the year it was made. Sasebo?? Isn't that where the US Navy has a base? I will be living in Hokkiado close to Tomakomai. <P>------------------<BR>87 Fiero GT V8 (coming soon)<BR>90 Eagle Talon Tsi Awd<BR>95 Eagle Talon Tsi Awd<BR>rashaam@hotmail.com<p>[This message has been edited by Rashaam (edited 04-22-2001).]||||reg||1
